# Git integration

`-L` / `--label` names the inputs (like `diff -L`), first left, then right.

```console
$ mydiff -L old -L new a.txt b.txt
? 1
--- old
+++ new
@@ -1,2 +1,2 @@
 one
-two
+2

$ mydiff -L 1 -L 2 -L 3 a.txt b.txt
? 2
mydiff: error: --label can be given at most twice (left, then right)

```

`mydiff git setup` prints the git config to install. Its exact text is
checked by `tests/git.rs`, which installs it and runs real git commands.

`mydiff git external` is git's external diff driver. It labels files by
repository path and exits 0 even when they differ, because git treats any
other status as a crash.

```console
$ mydiff git external a.txt a.txt 1111111 100644 b.txt 2222222 100644
diff --git a/a.txt b/a.txt
--- a/a.txt
+++ b/a.txt
@@ -1,2 +1,2 @@
 one
-two
+2

$ mydiff git external a.txt a.txt 1 100644 b.txt 2 100644 b.txt
? 2
mydiff: error: expected the 7 or 9 arguments git passes to an external diff, got 8

```
